A||||6||sloth85GT||HOME FROM VANCOUVER!!!||||10||
Z||000000||sloth85GT||08-29-2001||03:34 AM||||WOW, what an amazing trip I had, 9 days away from home with my lady. We first drove straight to Vancouver from Winnipeg, took us about 26 hours because we stopped for a little bit of food here and there. That was hell, driving all night. I didn't take my Fiero, that stayed home, we took my gf's 98 Hyandai Accent, not the best of cars, but I have to admit, it was AWESOME on gas. It cost us $90 in gas to get to Vancouver. When we got there, we pretty much slept.<P>My next 4 days there it rained! That sucked, but it didn't really slow us down. We went to the Science Center where I got my picture taked beside the Molson Indy Viper Pace car. Then the Vancouver Aquarium, the Capilano Suspension Bridge, took the sky tram up to the top of Grouse Mountain. <P>It was awesome. Our hotel was right on Robson street (basically their version of Portage Avenue in winnipeg). <P>Then from Vancouver, we drove to Calgary to stay 3 nights. We visited the Calgary Zoo and went up to Drumhellar. If you've never been to Drumhellar Vancouver, you HAVE to go.<BR>It was the best part of the trip. It's in the badlands, an almost desert like area that actually has rattle snakes in it. The Royal Tyrell Dinosaur Museum is there, it's amazing, from fossils to full size dinosaur reconstructions, it's great. And the whole town of Drumhellar has little Dinos all of the place on the street corners. That was the best $1000 I've ever spent!<P>------------------<BR>  <IMG SRC="http://www.mts.net/~kuzma/fieronl.gif">  <BR>Dan<BR>1985 Silver GT<P>WITH THE NEW WHEELS!!!!! WOOHOO!!!!!!||||reg||10
